  m_text: Protozoa is a group of microscopic, single-celled organisms that belong
    to the kingdom Protista and are commonly found in water, soil, and inside other
    living organisms as parasites or symbionts. They have diverse shapes and structures,
    can move using flagella, cilia, or pseudopodia, and obtain energy in various
    ways, such as ingesting organic matter or absorbing nutrients from their environment.
